50 insane new ways to use GPT-6, with Astra and the new ChatGPT Images 2.5 model
🎬 Try Images 2.5 in Artlist: https://artlist.io/?artlist_aid=aiSamson_3925&utm_source=affiliate_p&utm_medium=aiSamson_3925&utm_campaign=aiSamson_3925

Thanks to Artlist for sponsoring this video

All fifty with every link and prompt, plus ten you can run tonight:
https://delightfuldesign.eo.page/gpt6-fifty

GPT-6 Astra launched on 3 September and ChatGPT Images 2.5 followed on 8 September. This is the best of the first week: games built in days, a robot arm that paints with real paint, cameras that read football matches and warehouses, a font made from a poster, proteins that do not exist in nature, robots that learn from one video, a livestream that never ends, and a 90 year old maths problem with the proof checked by Astra. Every example is credited to the person who made it, below.

CORRECTION: The Zelda footage shown in the intro is official game footage, not a game created with Astra. I mistakenly presented it as an AI-made project. I’ve removed the explanation from the middle of the video, but the clip remains in the intro. I’m sorry for the error, and thank you to those who flagged it.

For a separate Zelda-inspired prototype, see The Legend of Astra by @lofihashbloom. The creator describes using Astra alongside Unity, Blender and Tripo, with development details in the replies:
https://x.com/lofihashbloom/status/2096064140510970318

This is a different project from the footage included in this video.

